{
  "name": "stork",
  "kind": "parts",
  "_about": "a white stork on the meadow: tall and white, the black flight feathers along the folded wing's rear half, the long straight red bill, long red legs, the neck carried straight and a little forward (2026-11-08 evening, named.py stork) The BILL: the lower mandible re-pointed as the crane's -- it ended 5 cm short of the upper's tip, cut off blunt; now a sharp `horn` along the commissure under the upper, tapering steadily to a point 5 mm behind and just under the upper's tip. (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sweep/necks.py) The NECK is one `sweep` (sculpt.js) along the chain of neck bones, not a tube a bone blended into the next: no bead at the joints. (2026-11-08, tools/creaturegen/sweep/flynecks.py) ALOFT the neck is held nearly straight ahead with a slight sag: the neck sweep is skinned from the body along its bones with its hand-offs on the rest curve's bends (`knotsAt`, `spread`), and the neck bones' and head's `flyRot` set with them.",
